{"title":"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the sum of the distinct positive prime divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15102760e73d77bc453dd7c1ad1c47cfa4783b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(12) = 2+3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/49036a2a92114dc127b611873cc1cda3e33dc4d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(101) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />). Evaluate the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/85318927de1c95868ff8ab5c05d4140487bd0c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)+f(2)+\\cdots+f(99)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b81097ac54e434963766001e47caa1dcd88003fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is internally tangent to a larger circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f7a9875557179ece650016df1cc310df671c71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> such that the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />. A diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is drawn tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />. A second line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> is drawn from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />. Let the line tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64baf3123325e36642571177d9b5e41aeafaf64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\emph hailstone$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4552b920136787482a4018f7ee59527af6d55085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = d_1d_2 \\cdots d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> denotes the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th digit in the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b6ab1bc82266a6badd3ad9c88ce3d5c4a2a5af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1,2, \\ldots,k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />, is a positive integer with distinct nonzero digits such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/449526b1a01fb05b0ab5d424f8afdf4bb2f5982a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_m &lt; d_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/801c9ca1235a588e4633fbfa1dd9b01bfe7fbb7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_m &gt; d_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a76a4272a950838c40808ef4e9bec29adca6020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 1,2,\\ldots,k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" /> (and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/846eaf79ee050d250a83709e19a95b381d780ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_0 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of four-digit hailstone numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of three-digit hailstone numbers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3afcb3ae698b232912beaad990c9e80781672b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; m \\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43a9078548a7167fe92632e8e9d74e94639f240a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; n \\le 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f697eae3bb5180fba554d9b23510c904b039faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\log_m{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a6632ff5742d435f382d5923349abdd1070b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\log_n{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />, find the number of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe213bc3ff14dfa400ebd207661a452c3b54103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\lfloor x \\rfloor = \\lceil y \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" />. (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4557d136477be7dedade03795960d759e03c80eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor a \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/8338bebc2a84d457bd0eae5f4100834b0b28aaa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil a \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"19\" /> is the least integer greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />).\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the largest prime divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b68c283de78bcb7e2500988305fc1c59843310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25^2+72^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9090f2e6bd5da465fea10a8c755d64e9185f61f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are polynomials defined by: \n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac76e3ac64058717f69456c8ee3d7e2ab671560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1(x) = 1+x+x^3+x^4+\\cdots+x^{96}+x^{97}+x^{99}+x^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"425\" height=\"19\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/640b7dea2df47826503e66747bf32c737d721131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2(x) = 1-x+x^2-\\cdots-x^{99}+x^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"291\" height=\"19\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1df9e316c28a2e078ac12724bb3682f1935422b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3(x) = 1+x+x^2+\\cdots+x^{66}+x^{67}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"285\" height=\"19\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Find the number of distinct complex roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e49b7c274e2b8c9f1cc3a267dfb4c766686455f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 \\cdot P_2 \\cdot P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A coin of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is flipped onto an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58a4fa43c595b7d97db5c954aef623ea91ab739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500 \\times 500$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" /> square grid divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b32623c3d21608acb59f855590c5b920018645a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2500$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> equal squares. Circles are inscribed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b32623c3d21608acb59f855590c5b920018645a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2500$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> squares. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> be the probability that, given that the coin lands completely within one of the smaller squares, it also lands completely within one of the circles. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the probability that, when flipped onto the grid, the coin lands completely within one of the smaller squares. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f0c6d216bb63a89845904c513ec0007b6b3e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75aa7191374607aea2f02836298203ebba8368cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n &gt; P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfacb9efc6606573c6c97b94ee9625d67bae215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n_0}{3} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a polyhedron with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> faces, all of which are equilateral triangles, squares, or regular pentagons with equal side length. Given there is at least one of each type of face and there are twice as many pentagons as triangles, what is the sum of all the possible number of vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can have?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> nondistinguishable residents are moving into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct houses in Conformistville, with at least one resident per house. In how many ways can the residents be assigned to these houses such that there is at least one house with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> residents?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22ccfc078c296ff9830df98685086d47770637ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle {2n \\choose n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"44\" height=\"53\" /> is divisible by all the primes between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a subset of consecutive elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c469a2bc6bdbbe6569db69002aaa3553b82dd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{n, n+1, \\ldots, n+999\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cb44cc081cf9d095cbe703dba5b39b889bf47d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\mu(A) = \\sum_{k \\in A} \\tau(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"125\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6bca5ee6c1c6c360b4a7b5efc02ee9dc60cd78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(k) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has an odd number of divisors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e11239192115678961d3ab5a3714649b2164425d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(k) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has an even number of divisors. For how many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a730c57d195380061aff83b0aab3d0de5288bc84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\le 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> does there exist an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d7f1b49ac64cbe98571e19d1c34a6b2b6a52ee2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| = 620$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5d213d95bdaa5fd820519512537b3489324cc0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu(A) = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />? (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/29680a0e11fad163e3a724436f78a84ae70d098a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|X|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the cardinality of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, or the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca8d0ec6dc74f13176a38469882c5e79894f7409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15ce28968754a7ce34595935f04929c46f99d0e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98d2ed450f84fb3b2599ba598ed5e6e7a69ecfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43bd901ceef2813942d8332e64f32195ea261ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = CE$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" />. Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> to meet the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2c1fd8b6b6ba7d523f53ad687a09c7858a13e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9ef6dcf44361a3f87e0e5bbfcfeb944f56a4fae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of positive integers with only odd digits satisfying the following condition: any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/4045d6bc2de65aea75286ad613b46fa5a699559d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digits must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> smallest elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Find the remainder upon dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70cbd8db4713b2f5cb1275db6c0227aadbdbb5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 68$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6ee794f92385fcf7f655997c5eb8fd4d01e4b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7b64e36d95e3783dec792c6d796e3a1e5e0098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle CA = 112$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> (intersection of the altitudes). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are constructed on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83ea2b2676b83c9afe2618c57a9c107b0e1d19d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HD$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/7381d73a5fd25fe335bba4cd0b2219adaf09ed3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HE$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afc06fe8fc84a5bb77c3c983754a09508fe2e5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HF$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/3553e6f3a5124ee804d45fe717ebb38971eab40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XH$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fb4a1b60fd67a3ee89710f7d762033724f81ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c0be96ca4bf306f1bef4e64e8597e8320626136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ZH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2a5d7d69ebec6dc196067fc3148e5f4a2ebd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX+BY+CZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d1216dd3855e1bb88b6136b4ce49c58b57747417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2006$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> colored beads are placed on a necklace (circular ring) such that each bead is adjacent to two others. The beads are labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820332d75715e0966c46780224431503de43b34a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2005}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"10\" /> around the circle in order. Two beads <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> are non-negative integers, satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/eda8881f130a4e10be6eab9663cb6526ed1bf3db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i = a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if the color of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is the same as the color of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />. Given that there exists no non-negative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83acea62fcc41cc5383b7abbb8192af8e4722d5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; 2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" /> and positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/36028d26540f03f967194cf4013848b578103999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 1003$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/020188740b2328b3a14149ca6638539c9bad14a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m = a_{m-n} = a_{m+n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"12\" />, where all subscripts are taken <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8dd7fddfe70c61b06c1020beda07520c26fef844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, find the minimum number of different colors of beads on the necklace.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME\" title=\"Mock AIME\">Mock AIME</a></li>\n<li>A <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wangsblog.com/jeffrey/MockAIME5.pdf\">.pdf</a> version of the problems</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006\">Mock AIME 5 2005-2006</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=76847\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2005-2006\">Mock AIME 4 2005-2006</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007\">Mock AIME 1 2006-2007</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018100329\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.066 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 951/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1383/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 225/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 29003/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.022      1 Template:Mock_AIME_box\n100.00%    7.022      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3956:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018100329 and revision id 13493. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}